From: Capri NixOS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] cmd: bootmenu: return to Capri menu after commands

Recreate the untimed main menu after a diagnostic command or generation
picker returns, without recursive run menucmd calls. The built-in console
entry still exits; the six-second delay applies only on first entry.

--- a/cmd/bootmenu.c
+++ b/cmd/bootmenu.c
@@ -700,6 +700,16 @@
 	if (delay_str)
 		delay = (int)simple_strtol(delay_str, NULL, 10);
 
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MOTOROLA_CAPRI)) {
+		int ret;
+
+		do {
+			ret = bootmenu_show(uefi, delay);
+			delay = -1;
+		} while (ret != BOOTMENU_RET_QUIT);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	bootmenu_show(uefi, delay);
 	return 0;
 }
